  <project_license>MIT</project_license>
  <name>npad</name>
  <summary>A lightweight Notepad-style text editor</summary>
  <description>
    <p>
      npad is a small, fast text editor inspired by classic Windows Notepad.
      It opens instantly, keeps each file's encoding and line endings intact,
      and saves atomically so a failed save never destroys the existing file.
    </p>
    <p>
      It adds only quality-of-life features that do not change how Notepad
      behaves: undo history, word wrap, zoom, a status bar, colour schemes and
      crash recovery.
    </p>
  </description>
